00:16:14,220 --> 00:16:15,970
Basically, we just feel that he's, uh...

257
00:16:16,220 --> 00:16:17,260
We hate that guy.

258
00:16:17,550 --> 00:16:18,720
We hate him.

259
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:20,470
We're sorry, Pheebs.

260
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:21,980
Uh-huh. Okay.

261
00:16:22,230 --> 00:16:25,560
Don't you think maybe it's just that he's so perceptive...

262
00:16:25,810 --> 00:16:27,440
...that it freaked you out?

263
00:16:27,650 --> 00:16:29,440
- No, I hate him.     - No, we hate him.

264
00:16:29,650 --> 00:16:30,820
I'm sorry.

265
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:45,790
Ma. What are you doing here?

266
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,040
I came to give you this...

267
00:16:48,290 --> 00:16:49,540
- ...and this.     - Ow.

268
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:51,250
Big ring.

269
00:16:51,590 --> 00:16:54,550
Why did you fill your father's head with that garbage...

270
00:16:54,800 --> 00:16:57,430
...about making things right?

271
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:59,930
Things were fine the way they were.

272
00:17:00,180 --> 00:17:02,850
There's chicken in there. Put it away.

273
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:05,980
For God's sake, Joey. Really.

274
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,980
Hold on. You knew?

275
00:17:10,190 --> 00:17:12,570
Of course I knew. What do you think?

276
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:15,190
Your father is no James Bond.

277
00:17:15,450 --> 00:17:17,280
You should have heard his cover stories.

278
00:17:17,530 --> 00:17:19,780
"I'm sleeping over at my accountant's."

279
00:17:20,030 --> 00:17:22,290
I mean, what is that? Please.

280
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:24,370
So then, how could you...?

281
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:27,080
Do you remember how your father used to be?

282
00:17:27,330 --> 00:17:31,540
Always yelling. Nothing made him happy.

283
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:35,510
Not that wood shop, not those stupid little ships in the bottle.

284
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:37,260
Now he's happy.

285
00:17:37,510 --> 00:17:40,490
I mean, it's nice. He has a hobby.

286
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:46,020
Ma, I don't mean to be disrespectful, but...

287
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,440
...what the hell are you talking about?

288
00:17:49,730 --> 00:17:53,010
- I mean, what about you?     - Me? I'm fine.

289
00:17:53,360 --> 00:17:54,610
Look, honey...

290
00:17:54,990 --> 00:17:57,070
...in an ideal world...

291
00:17:57,360 --> 00:18:00,930
...there'd be no her and your father would look like Sting.

292
00:18:02,910 --> 00:18:04,580
And I'll tell you something else:

293
00:18:04,790 --> 00:18:08,160
Ever since that poodle-stuffer came along...

294
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:12,710
...he's been so ashamed of himself that he's been more attentive.

295
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,800
He's been more loving.

296
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:17,550
It's like every day is our anniversary.

297
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:20,180
I'm happy for you?

298
00:18:20,390 --> 00:18:21,590
Well, don't be.

299
00:18:22,640 --> 00:18:24,510
Because now everything's screwed up.

300
00:18:26,020 --> 00:18:30,270
I just want it the way it was.

301
00:18:30,520 --> 00:18:33,400
Ma, I'm sorry.

302
00:18:33,650 --> 00:18:37,110
I just did what I thought you'd want.

303
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:41,280
I know you did, cookie. Oh, I know you did.

304
00:18:44,240 --> 00:18:45,660
So tell me...

305
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:48,560
Did you see her?

306
00:18:49,710 --> 00:18:50,790
Yeah.

307
00:18:51,790 --> 00:18:54,340
You're 10 times prettier than she is.

308
00:18:54,550 --> 00:18:55,880
That's sweet.

309
00:18:57,710 --> 00:18:59,470
Could I take her?

310
00:19:00,760 --> 00:19:03,470
With this ring, no contest.

311
00:19:07,140 --> 00:19:09,390
- What's wrong, sweetie?     - Nothing.

312
00:19:09,730 --> 00:19:12,150
No, no. What's wrong? Come on.

313
00:19:12,350 --> 00:19:13,770
Okay.

314
00:19:17,030 --> 00:19:18,780
It's nothing. I'm fine.

315
00:19:18,990 --> 00:19:20,950
It's just, um... It's my friends.

316
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:23,870
They have a liking problem with you...

317
00:19:24,120 --> 00:19:25,320
...in that, um...

318
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:26,950
...they don't.

319
00:19:29,370 --> 00:19:31,750
Oh. They don't?

320
00:19:32,790 --> 00:19:34,040
But you know...

321
00:19:34,290 --> 00:19:37,090
...they don't see all of the wonderfulness that I see.

322
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:40,840
They don't see all the good stuff and all the sweet stuff.

323
00:19:41,090 --> 00:19:42,630
They think you're a little...

324
00:19:43,510 --> 00:19:46,600
- What?     - Intense and creepy.

325
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:49,850
Oh.

326
00:19:50,020 --> 00:19:52,640
But I don't. Me. Phoebe.

327
00:19:54,860 --> 00:19:57,110
Well, I'm not at all surprised they feel that way.

328
00:19:57,320 --> 00:19:59,730
You're not? See, that's why you're so great.

329
00:20:00,110 --> 00:20:02,240
Actually, it's quite typical behavior...

330
00:20:02,490 --> 00:20:06,660
...when you have this kind of dysfunctional group dynamic.

331
00:20:06,870 --> 00:20:09,490
You know, this kind of codependent...

332
00:20:09,750 --> 00:20:11,370
...emotionally stunted...

333
00:20:11,660 --> 00:20:16,790
...sitting in your stupid coffeehouse, with your stupid big cups...

334
00:20:17,040 --> 00:20:20,780
...which, I'm sorry, might as well have nipples on them.

335
00:20:21,840 --> 00:20:26,300
And you're all like, "Oh, define me. Define me.

336
00:20:26,510 --> 00:20:29,310
Love me. I need love."

337
00:20:30,810 --> 00:20:32,430
So you talked to your dad, huh?

338
00:20:32,640 --> 00:20:35,890
Yeah. He's gonna keep cheating on Ma, like she wanted.

339
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:38,520
Ma's gonna keep pretending she doesn't know even though she does.

340
00:20:38,770 --> 00:20:41,530
And my sister Tina can't see her husband anymore...

341
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:43,820
...because he got a restraining order.

342
00:20:44,660 --> 00:20:48,070
Which has nothing to do with it, except that I found out today.

343
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:49,280
Wow.

344
00:20:49,450 --> 00:20:52,080
Things sure have changed here on Walton's mountain.

345
00:20:54,250 --> 00:20:55,410
So, Joey, are you okay?

346
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,170
Yeah, I guess.

347
00:20:57,420 --> 00:20:59,670
It's just... You know, they're parents.

348
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:02,880
After a certain point, you gotta let go.

349
00:21:03,380 --> 00:21:04,760
Even if you know better...

350
00:21:04,970 --> 00:21:07,470
...you gotta let them make their own mistakes.

351
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:08,720
And just think...

352
00:21:08,930 --> 00:21:11,060
...in a couple years, we get to turn into them.

353
00:21:11,310 --> 00:21:12,680
Oh, please.

354
00:21:12,930 --> 00:21:15,520
If I turn into my parents, I'll either be an alcoholic blond...

355
00:21:15,690 --> 00:21:18,770
...chasing after 20-year-old boys...

356
00:21:19,020 --> 00:21:20,820
...or I'll end up like my mom.

357
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:26,860
- Hey.     - Hey, Pheebs.

358
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:28,530
How's it going?

359
00:21:29,660 --> 00:21:32,030
Okay, except I broke up with Roger.

360
00:21:32,290 --> 00:21:33,790
Oh.

361
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:35,120
Yeah, right.

362
00:21:35,290 --> 00:21:37,920
No, no, really. Aw.

363
00:21:39,210 --> 00:21:42,920
- What happened?     - Ugh. I don't know. I mean...

364
00:21:43,130 --> 00:21:44,630
He's a good person...

365
00:21:44,880 --> 00:21:46,760
...and he can be really sweet.

366
00:21:47,380 --> 00:21:50,260
And in some ways, I think he is so right for me.

367
00:21:50,510 --> 00:21:53,430
It's just, I hate that guy.

368
00:22:00,650 --> 00:22:03,110
Hey, Joey. What's going on?

369
00:22:03,360 --> 00:22:05,990
Clear the tracks for the boobie payback express.

370
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:08,430
Next stop, Rachel Green.

371
00:22:14,370 --> 00:22:16,750
Joey, what the hell were you doing?

372
00:22:17,250 --> 00:22:19,540
Sorry, wrong boobies.

373
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:33,890
Hello, Joey.

374
00:22:35,430 --> 00:22:36,640
Hello, dear.

